msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:9
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:13
msgid "Show frontend templates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:14
msgid ""
"When enabled, the information you defined for each item will be nicely "
"displayed in a list on the item page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:21
msgid "GBFS Default Vehicle Types"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:22
msgid ""
"When publishing additional vehicle information to the GBFS API, some "
"information is required, otherwise the data published will be considered "
"invalid. Therefore, you can set default values here, that will be taken "
"when the values are not defined at the item level. Items can also be hidden "
"from the API, when the checkbox is set in the corresponding item."
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:26
msgid "Default form factor"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:28
msgid "The default form factor that is used when none is defined at the item level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:35
msgid "Default propulsion type"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:37
msgid ""
"The default propulsion type that is used when none is defined at the item "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:44
msgid "Default max range (meters)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/OptionsArray.php:46
msgid ""
"When a motor is defined in the propulsion type, a max range also has to be "
"given."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:20
msgid "Form factor"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:21
msgid ""
"The item's general form factor. When none is defined the defaults from the "
"settings will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:30
msgid "Propulsion type"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:31
msgid ""
"The primary propulsion type of the vehicle. When none is defined the "
"defaults from the settings will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:40
msgid "Range (meters) (required when using a motor)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:41
msgid ""
"The range the vehicle can travel with a full charge / tank. When none is "
"defined the defaults from the settings will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:52
msgid "Wheel count"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:53
msgid "Number of wheels this vehicle has"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:64
msgid "Max permitted speed (km/h)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:65
msgid ""
"The maximum speed in kilometers per hour this vehicle is permitted to reach "
"in accordance with local permit and regulations."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:76
msgid "Cargo volume capacity (l)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:77
msgid ""
"Cargo volume available in the vehicle, expressed in liters. For cars, it "
"corresponds to the space between the boot floor, including the storage "
"under the hatch, to the rear shelf in the trunk."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:88
msgid "Cargo load capacity (kg)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:89
msgid ""
"The capacity of the vehicle cargo space (excluding passengers), expressed "
"in kilograms."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:100
msgid "Empty weight (kg)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:101
msgid "The weight of the vehicle when it is empty."
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:112
msgid "Length (cm)"
msgstr ""

#: src/WordPress/CustomPostType/Item.php:113
msgid ""
"The minimum length of the vehicle. For trailers, the length with the "
"trailer drawbar folded in."
msgstr ""

